ent we have for the painful phase, and research shows it can significantly reduce your pain and improve your ability to participate in therapy. We do need to watch your blood sugar closely afterward. Would you like to try that today?\'\n\n**6. Reinforce the partnership**:\n\'I am not giving up on you, and I do not want you to give up on the process. If you would like a second opinion, I fully support that — I can refer you to a shoulder specialist. My goal is for you to feel confident in your care plan. Let us adjust our approach and continue working together through this.\'\n\n**Key principles demonstrated**: Empathy, validation without defensiveness, honest prognostication, willingness to investigate patient concerns, treatment escalation, collaborative decision-making, openness to second opinion.',
